WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.768
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.068 --> 00:00:09.617
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.917 --> 00:00:16.958
Unit eighteen: Formal Letters and Emails. Today you will write a clear formal letter or application email.

4
00:00:17.258 --> 00:00:19.759
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.165
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:25.739
Formal.

7
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.947
Formal means polite and serious.

8
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.120
Use formal language.

9
00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:34.137
Your turn. Say: Formal.

10
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:37.908
Formal.

11
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:39.848
Application.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.045
Application means a request for a job or place.

13
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.197
I send an application.

14
00:00:46.783 --> 00:00:49.575
Your turn. Say: Application.

15
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:53.504
Application.

16
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.448
Sincerely.

17
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.053
Sincerely means in an honest way.

18
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:00.930
Yours sincerely.

19
00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:04.123
Your turn. Say: Sincerely.

20
00:01:06.967 --> 00:01:08.188
Sincerely.

21
00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:09.905
Faithfully.

22
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.520
Faithfully means used when you do not know the name.

23
00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:15.466
Yours faithfully.

24
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.760
Your turn. Say: Faithfully.

25
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.508
Faithfully.

26
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.414
Enclose.

27
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:27.648
Enclose means to include with a letter.

28
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.808
I enclose my CV.

29
00:01:30.417 --> 00:01:32.779
Your turn. Say: Enclose.

30
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:36.785
Enclose.

31
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.818
Opportunity.

32
00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:41.654
Opportunity means a chance.

33
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.041
Thank you for this opportunity.

34
00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:47.314
Your turn. Say: Opportunity.

35
00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.342
Opportunity.

36
00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:53.119
Request.

37
00:01:54.117 --> 00:01:56.221
Request means to ask politely.

38
00:01:56.817 --> 00:01:58.677
I request more information.

39
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:02.063
Your turn. Say: Request.

40
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.878
Request.

41
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:07.583
Reply.

42
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:10.060
Reply means an answer.

43
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.533
I look forward to your reply.

44
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.116
Your turn. Say: Reply.

45
00:02:18.967 --> 00:02:19.945
Reply.

46
00:02:20.733 --> 00:02:24.431
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.283 --> 00:02:27.585
Visal, how do I start a formal letter?

48
00:02:28.683 --> 00:02:38.731
Write Dear Sir or Madam if you do not know the name, or Dear Mr. Lee if you do. Then give the reason for writing in the first paragraph.

49
00:02:39.817 --> 00:02:41.421
What language should I use?

50
00:02:42.517 --> 00:02:51.346
Use polite phrases and full forms, such as I would like to apply and I am writing to enquire. Do not use slang or short forms like don't.

51
00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:53.521
How do I end it?

52
00:02:54.617 --> 00:03:05.547
Say I look forward to your reply. Close with Yours faithfully if you began with Dear Sir or Madam, or Yours sincerely if you used a name, then sign.

53
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.328
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.183 --> 00:03:11.647
Grammar focus: formal letter layout.

55
00:03:11.947 --> 00:03:13.273
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.983 --> 00:03:16.900
I am writing to apply for the position of assistant.

57
00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:19.630
I look forward to your reply.

58
00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:27.886
Begin with a polite greeting, state the purpose, give clear details and end with a suitable closing. Avoid slang and short forms.

59
00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.744
Be careful! Don't say: Hi, I wanna apply.

60
00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.953
Say: Dear Sir or Madam, I am writing to apply.

61
00:03:37.253 --> 00:03:38.754
Use formal language.

62
00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:42.300
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.391
An Application.

64
00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:48.084
Kunthea writes a formal email to apply for a library job.

65
00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.158
She begins with Dear Sir or Madam.

66
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.932
She explains her skills and encloses her CV.

67
00:03:55.933 --> 00:03:57.933
She thanks them for the opportunity.

68
00:03:58.933 --> 00:04:01.130
She ends with Yours faithfully and her name.

69
00:04:02.233 --> 00:04:06.142
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:06.983 --> 00:04:09.250
Dear Sir or Madam ends with Yours blank.

71
00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.343
A, faithfully. B, sincerely. C, friends.

72
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.109
The answer is A: faithfully.

73
00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.168
A formal letter avoids blank.

74
00:04:22.468 --> 00:04:25.762
A, dates. B, slang. C, greetings.

75
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.218
The answer is B: slang.

76
00:04:32.383 --> 00:04:34.244
I look forward to your blank.

77
00:04:34.544 --> 00:04:38.394
A, slang. B, food. C, reply.

78
00:04:41.933 --> 00:04:44.223
The answer is C: reply.

79
00:04:45.383 --> 00:04:46.988
Enclose means blank.

80
00:04:47.288 --> 00:04:50.976
A, include. B, delete. C, hide.

81
00:04:54.533 --> 00:04:56.336
The answer is A: include.

82
00:04:57.483 --> 00:04:59.564
Kunthea applies for a blank job.

83
00:04:59.864 --> 00:05:03.343
A, farm. B, library. C, kitchen.

84
00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.573
The answer is B: library.

85
00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:14.545
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:15.383 --> 00:05:17.406
Write a formal opening sentence.

87
00:05:26.217 --> 00:05:27.810
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:35.862
I am writing to apply for the position of library assistant. I enclose my CV. I look forward to your reply.

89
00:05:36.162 --> 00:05:37.975
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:38.883 --> 00:05:43.463
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and formal letter layout.

91
00:05:43.763 --> 00:05:48.633
Today's value is good manners. Say please and thank you, and be polite to everyone.

92
00:05:48.933 --> 00:05:51.515
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:51.815 --> 00:05:55.025
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

